# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies
/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# testing
/coverage

# next.js
# (no trailing slash, so a `.next` SYMLINK to an off-iCloud cache is ignored too)
/.next
/out/

# production
/build

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# env files (can opt-in for committing if needed)
.env*
!.env.example

# vercel
.vercel

# supabase CLI local state (e.g. the linked-project file)
supabase/.temp/

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# Dev cache symlinked from .next, kept off iCloud (ends in .nosync)
.next.nosync

# A friend's trading-bot market data. Nothing to do with Trackd — it lives here
# only so Adrian still has it to hand. Kept OUT of git deliberately: it is 7 MB
# of CSV that was once committed by accident, and adding a .gitignore rule does
# NOT untrack an already-committed file (that took a `git rm --cached` to undo).
# Do not remove these rules without knowing that.
/trading data/
condensed_GLBX-*

# iCloud's conflicted-copy duplicates. Syncing this folder through iCloud Drive
# leaves a "<name> 2.<ext>" beside a file it thinks diverged — 102 appeared in a
# single session. They are byte-copies of tracked files, never edited, and
# committing them both doubles the repo and confuses git's rename detection
# (it starts pairing real files with the copies). Delete them freely.
* 2.*
* 2

# The verification harness. Rebuilt per session, drives PRODUCTION Supabase and
# real Stripe, and holds nothing worth keeping between sessions.
#
# `/scratchpad/*` rather than `/scratchpad/`, because git cannot re-include
# anything whose PARENT DIRECTORY is excluded — the negation below is silently
# inert against the directory form.
/scratchpad/*

# ...except the test-clock harness, which IS worth keeping between sessions: it
# is the tooling spec 04's Steps 9 to 11 and Monday's three observations run on,
# and three cold reviewers need to be able to find it.
!/scratchpad/harness/

# ...and the SHARED SPINE every QA driver imports (D89, part one).
#
# ⚠️ THE CLASS THIS CLOSES WAS ALREADY FOUND ONCE. `lib/billing/gate.ts` records
# it about `gate-audit.mjs`: the script its credibility rested on "was on one
# machine and in nobody's clone". That was fixed for one file and the class was
# left open — so every `qa-*.mjs` and `cold-*.mjs` driver, and the spine they all
# import, is still untracked. Evidence that 05 §5 and 12 rest on cannot be re-run
# by a cold reviewer or by a future session.
#
# This is the piece whose loss would be worst and it is one file: the service
# client, `makeUser`, `signIn`, and `dropUser` with its BY ID ONLY guard. It holds
# NO secret — it reads `.env.local` at runtime — and no banned technique. Scanned
# before tracking.
#
# The drivers themselves are tracked AT THE FREEZE, not before, and only the ones
# backing a signed-off verification: the tree stops moving there, the full set
# exists, and ~60 files landing mid-build is the churn that muddied a review round
# once already. Each is secret-scanned first, and anything that patches a list or
# calls a billing-writing route is stripped or left out rather than committed as a
# recipe for the next session to copy.
#
# ⚠️ NOTE ON SCOPE: `05` Step 7's evidence is a test-clock scenario, so it lands in
# `harness/` and is TRACKED THE MOMENT IT IS WRITTEN. It is outside part two
# entirely. The same is true of `04` Steps 9 to 11 and of `11` Steps 4 and 5
# (`reconcile.scenario.ts`). Part two is only the `.mjs` browser drivers.
#
# ⚠️ AND NO CREDENTIAL LIVES IN ANY TRACKED FILE. The QA fixture password moved to
# `.env.local` as `QA_TEST_PASSWORD`; `admin.mjs` and `harness/core.ts` both read
# it and throw if it is unset. It only ever applied to `@trackd-qa.invalid`
# accounts torn down by id, but a credential in a repository is a question
# somebody has to answer later.
!/scratchpad/admin.mjs

# ⚠️ AND THE READ-ONLY DRIVER, tracked 2026-08-18 BEFORE 08 rather than at the
# freeze. It is the 23/23 evidence for the cohorts `08` must be re-verified
# against — the read-only pop-up's copy, its mechanics, D28's destination — and it
# existed on ONE MACHINE, in nobody's clone, which is the exact failure
# `lib/billing/gate.ts` already records about `gate-audit.mjs`: "the script this
# paragraph rests its credibility on was on one machine and in nobody's clone".
#
# Secret-scanned before tracking: no key, no token, no password. It takes the QA
# password from `admin.mjs`, which reads `.env.local` and throws if unset, and it
# deletes its one account BY ID in a `finally`. The `/api/billing/reconcile` probe
# it used to carry was stripped: it called a billing route, asserted nothing, and
# its comment claimed to establish something a status code cannot.
!/scratchpad/qa-05-readonly.mjs

# ⚠️ BUT NEVER THE SINK'S KEY MATERIAL. `PushSink` self-signs a certificate for
# 127.0.0.1 on first run and caches it here. It is regenerated on demand, it is
# worthless to anybody, and a private key does not go in a repository regardless.
/scratchpad/harness/.certs/
